--
-- Act I: Window Interaction
--
PRIMARY_NARRATOR: Rain tracks down the glass in jagged grey veins. Across the courtyard, dark chimneys leak soot into the drowning twilight.
CHRONIC_SHAME: Look at them out there. Moving between doorways with purpose, collars pulled up against the cold. They have places to be. People expecting them. You haven't stepped past the landing in a week.
NOSTALGIC_ACHE: Remember when the rain smelled like asphalt and possibility? In the capital, before the inquest. Before every streetlamp started looking like a verdict.
CYNICAL_DETACHMENT: A pathetic tableau. Staring out the window like a tubercular poet. The city doesn't care that your mind is dissolving, Lilith. It has coal to burn.
PRIMARY_NARRATOR: The pane is freezing against your fingertips. Step back. The view isn't offering any absolution tonight. #end
